---
portal:
  portal:
    # A Pipeline's `secretRef` decrypts with SOPS and this instance's own age identity (T-4678),
    # never dev's. Operator-supplied, created once from the identity kept in `.secrets/`:
    #
    #   kubectl -n smartcity create secret generic portal-age-identity \
    #     --from-file=keys.txt=.secrets/age-prod.key
    #
    # Without it every reference is refused with "the age identity is unreadable" (fail closed).
    sopsAgeSecret: portal-age-identity
    # 2 min between runs. At the 60 s default each run republished all 97 datasets through the
    # public edge, about 1,000 requests a minute, while the edge still saw every caller as
    # 10.42.0.1 (T-4717, 05:25Z); the Portal now skips unchanged datasets (~630 requests a run,
    # 07:01Z). Not longer: this Portal has no forge webhook secret, so the timer is the only sync,
    # and after an apply the edge file waits for the first run of the new pod as leader.
    syncInterval: 120
